[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 20: differential 8-PSK.
# 8-DPSK sends three bits as a phase change of 0 to 315 degrees in steps of 45, so the matched-filter constellation shows eight points on a circle. With a 3 Hz carrier offset the circle spins, but each step between symbols stays near a multiple of 45 degrees, so a differential receiver still decodes. Compared with coherent 8-PSK it pays a noise penalty, and with eight points the margin between neighbours is only 22.5 degrees. Set CFO to 0 and compare.
Version=3
Modulation=8-DPSK
NumberOfSymbols=1024
SymbolRateBaud=1000
SamplesPerSymbol=8
Pulse=RRC
RRCBeta=0.2
SpanSymbols=10
AmplitudeGain=1
DataSource=Random
Seed=5489
Bits=
